    "doi": "10.1017/S0016756813000393",
    "citation": "García Muro, V. J., Rubinstein, C. V. & Steemans, P. 2014. Upper Silurian miospores from the Precordillera Basin, Argentina: biostratigraphic, palaeoenvironmental and palaeogeographic implications. Geological Magazine 151, 472–490.",
    "language": "English",
    "reports_window_spores": true,
    "comment": "The paper reports 14 productive samples and plots their taxon distributions in Figure 4. The extraction below captures the authors' combined formation-level list; it does not transcribe the individual sample assemblages and is therefore incomplete at sample resolution. Four samples closest to the upper boundary were barren. The authors favour a Ludlow age but cannot exclude Pridoli for the youngest samples; some taxa have previously been associated with the Lochkovian. Hispanaediscus wenlockensis may be reworked. Figure captions include several qualified identifications and Retusotriletes sp. in addition to the main taxonomic list."
  },
