      "age_basis": "mixed",
      "age_basis_detail": "Miospore correlations with Spanish biozones support Ludlow, with Pridoli not excluded for the youngest samples. Marine phytoplankton, including acritarchs, independently supports Ludlow. The paper discusses differing conodont and brachiopod age interpretations.",
      "age_circular": true,
      "stage_min_proposed": "Pridoli",
      "stage_max_proposed": "Gorstian",
      "setting_as_reported": "Shaly-predominant sediments of the lower part of the Los Espejos Formation represent a low-energy open shelf environment, followed towards the top by an increasing amount of sandstone beds, representing storm-dominated shelf and shoreface environments.",
      "setting_class": "marine-shelf",
      "n_samples": "14 productive samples; 18 collected",
      "reworking_status": "discussed",
      "notes": "This is the combined list for the two sampled intervals, not a claim that every taxon occurs in every sample. Figure 4 supplies sample-level distributions; continuous lines indicate identified species, dashed lines cf. identifications and dotted lines supposed ranges. The palynological assemblage is rich in marine acritarchs and chlorophytes. Hispanaediscus wenlockensis could be reworked. The authors include Clivosispora verrucata varieties in the Chelinospora verrucata var. verrucata morphon and propose Chelinospora poecilomorpha as a junior synonym.",
      "locator": "Sections 4–6; Figures 4–8; pp. 477–486",
